WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:12.270
On March 15th, 2011, Martin Sims was wandering
down the streets of Carson, California.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:16.810
His clothes were ragged, he was filthy, and
gibbering like a madman with a full beard

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:18.610
and long, unkempt hair.

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:23.090
His body was covered in scars, but he showed
no signs of malnutrition.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:25.400
What made Martin’s sudden appearance so
remarkable?

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.089
He’d been missing for three years.

00:00:28.089 --> 00:00:30.919
When he was interviewed by police, they asked
him where he’d been all this time.

00:00:30.919 --> 00:00:32.599
They couldn’t believe his answer.

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:35.770
He’d been trapped in an Ikea since 2008.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:40.280
But this was no ordinary Ikea – this was
a dangerous anomaly that would come to be

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:45.149
known as SCP-3008 .
Martin’s strange answers in his interview

00:00:45.149 --> 00:00:49.199
were laughed off by his interviewing officers,
who assumed he was either crazy or under the

00:00:49.199 --> 00:00:53.460
influence of something, but they caught the
attention of an SCP Foundation Field Agent

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:54.920
embedded in the precinct.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:59.130
The report was passed up the chain to a local
Site Director, who approved a detachment of

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:02.390
Foundation Field Operatives to look into Martin’s
case.

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:06.540
While he was reluctant to lead the Foundation
Agents back to the offending Ikea – the

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.280
Foundation can be extremely persuasive.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.360
His screams of “Please, I’m begging you,
don’t take me back!

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:16.580
Don’t make me go back!” were noted but
ultimately disregarded.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:21.820
When the SCP Foundation had triangulated the
position of SCP-3008 , which was indeed an

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:27.150
active Ikea, the entire retail zone was closed
and barricaded under the pretence of a severe

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:29.070
black mold infestation.

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:33.550
Armed Foundation Personnel also arrived on
site shortly after, based on Martin’s vague

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:36.240
statements that there were creatures of some
kind inside.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.750
Due to his deteriorating mental health, Martin
was unable to provide a great deal of lucid

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:46.860
information on the specific traits of SCP-3008
, but one phrase he kept repeating was “bigger

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.150
on the inside.”

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:51.990
Once researchers were satisfied that Martin
had delivered all the pertinent information

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:56.670
he was able to, he was administered Foundation
Amnestics to erase his memory of the last

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:59.020
three years and returned to his family.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:03.450
A cover story was formulated: Martin had been
kidnapped and abused for three years by a

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.910
mentally-unbalanced stalker in downtown Carson.

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:10.140
He’d been able to escape as said stalker
took his own life out of guilt – a suicide

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:14.540
that the Foundation expertly fabricated to
make their cover story airtight.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:18.440
With the loose end of Martin Sims taken care
of, the true observation of SCP-3008 could

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:19.440
begin.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:25.010
A base set around the perimeter of the mysterious
Ikea kept a 24-hour watch on the building,

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:27.230
covering all potential entrances and exits.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:31.510
No exploratory missions had yet been approved
by the Foundation ethics committee, so they

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:35.819
first wanted to perform a week of external
observation to see if any of the store’s

00:02:35.819 --> 00:02:39.180
anomalous properties extended beyond the confines
of the building.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.430
After a week of nothing, it appeared they
did not.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:46.239
A local Site Director approved the use of
twenty disposable Class-D Personnel to explore

00:02:46.239 --> 00:02:50.620
the interior of SCP-3008 .
The D-Class operatives would be split into

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:54.819
four squads of five men – Alpha, Bravo,
Charlie, and Delta Squad.

00:02:54.819 --> 00:02:58.300
Each would be assigned a different quadrant
of the store, and would deliver information

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:02.330
back to the control team on site via a live
audio and video link.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:06.290
Three of the four teams, upon entering the
store, reported nothing out of the ordinary.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:10.540
Neither the audio or video they were sending
back indicated anything different from a standard

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:14.459
Ikea store – from the flat-pack wardrobes
to the Swedish meatballs.

00:03:14.459 --> 00:03:19.519
Team Delta, however, suddenly began experiencing
a scrambled audio and video connection.

00:03:19.519 --> 00:03:22.430
Shortly after, communication with Team Delta
dropped off entirely.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:27.170
They disappeared somewhere inside the store,
and haven’t been seen since – with one

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:28.670
notable exception.

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:32.469
After the disappearance of the extraction
of teams, Foundation Researchers classified

00:03:32.469 --> 00:03:38.280
SCP-3008 as Euclid, because its anomalous
properties were at least confined to the interior

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.299
of the store.

00:03:39.299 --> 00:03:42.310
And even then, seemingly not the entire interior.

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:49.139
The anomalous area within SCP-3008 became
known as SCP-3008-1, and containment appeared

00:03:49.139 --> 00:03:50.969
to be 100% secure.

00:03:50.969 --> 00:03:54.830
There was no telling how many people had already
gone missing in the store over the years,

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.950
but the disappearances must be stopped.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:01.739
The Foundation maintained constant surveillance
around the perimeter of SCP-3008 , but it

00:04:01.739 --> 00:04:06.099
appeared they could prevent any further “incidents”
by simply preventing other civilians from

00:04:06.099 --> 00:04:07.799
accessing the Ikea store.

00:04:07.799 --> 00:04:12.069
Martin’s ravings about monsters were assumed
to just be the product of delirium.

00:04:12.069 --> 00:04:14.810
Until a surviving member of Delta Team suddenly
reappeared.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:17.250
The date was November 3rd, 2011.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:21.121
It was a cold night, a few hours after what
would have been closing time if the store

00:04:21.121 --> 00:04:25.390
were still active and seven months after the
extraction teams had disappeared somewhere

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:26.820
in the confines of SCP-3008.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:32.220
There had been no anomalous activity outside
the store since the perimeter was first secured,

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:36.780
and Foundation researchers hadn’t expected
that to change, until the last surviving member

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:39.680
of Delta Team came barging out of the store’s
entrance.

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:43.530
Startled Field Operatives were amazed to see
him again, but they were even more amazed

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:47.940
to see what was following him out of the store,
repeating the same phrase: “The store is

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:49.860
now closed, please exit the building.”

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:53.630
Despite the fact that the entity chasing the
Delta Team survivor was wearing the yellow

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:58.820
shirt and blue pants of an Ikea store employee,
the being was definitely not human.

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:02.110
It was around seven feet tall, with no visible
face.

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:07.120
The entity had grossly extended limbs – with
each arm being around five or six feet long,

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.500
and ending in a huge, oversized hand.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:13.750
The whole process was so sudden that the Field
Agents present at the perimeter weren’t

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:18.080
able to save the Delta Team survivor, as the
entity reached forward with its freakishly

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:22.110
long arms, grabbed him, and twisted his head
off like a child with a doll.

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:25.850
The Field Operatives present drew their weapons
and peppered the entity with bullets.

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:29.530
It would later be classified as SCP-3008-2.

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:33.621
The being appeared to collapse and die from
the physical trauma, at which point both it

00:05:33.621 --> 00:05:38.820
and the body of the former Delta Team survivor
were taken for an autopsy by Foundation researchers.

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:42.780
There were no biological abnormalities to
the body of the Delta Team survivor, so it

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:48.690
did not appear that the anomalous properties
of SCP-3008-1 had any effect on the physiology

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:49.780
of its occupants.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:53.710
He was not malnourished despite being missing
for months, and the contents of his stomach

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:59.800
looked to be half-digested food consistent
with the menu of a typical Ikea store restaurant.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:04.640
SCP-3008-2, on the other hand, raised a number
of perplexing biological questions.

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:08.440
The autopsy revealed that the creature’s
clothes were actually a part of its body,

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:10.160
like an additional layer of skin.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:13.410
The creature lacked blood or any kind of vascular
system.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:17.360
Even stranger, the entity didn’t appear
to have any bones or internal organs, not

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:18.920
even a brain or nervous system.

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:22.440
It was a being made entirely of skin, all
the way to its core.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:26.110
How it was able to move, or even live for
that matter, remains a mystery.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:29.680
Though when you work for The SCP Foundation,
you learn to accept that some things will

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:31.460
always remain unexplained.

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:35.440
One thing was certain, though: Martin Sims
was right about his monsters.

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:39.470
After the incident with Delta Team, the Foundation
deemed that sending manned explorations into

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:44.930
the heart of SCP-3008 was too much of a liability,
and planned a series of drone-based reconnaissance

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:46.440
missions into the anomaly.

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:50.300
The first of these drones experienced connection
issues and failed when attempting to venture

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.060
into the Ikea’s anomalous zone.

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:55.870
However, after a lengthy period of trial and
error, the Foundation was able to establish

00:06:55.870 --> 00:07:01.360
a more secure connection with its drones,
even when deep into the SCP-3008-1 anomalous

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:02.360
zone.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:06.310
It was only then that some of the most extraordinary
discoveries were made.

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:11.490
SCP-3008-1 seemed to break the laws of spatial
reality, as the area of the Ikea’s interior

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:15.300
was at least an order of magnitude larger
than its exterior.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:18.150
Just as Martin Sims had said: It was bigger
on the inside.

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:19.500
But just how much bigger?

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:23.221
The Foundation has yet to find evidence of
any physical terminators within the store

00:07:23.221 --> 00:07:27.050
that might indicate SCP-3008-1 has an “end
point.”

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:32.220
While an area of at least ten kilometres squared
has been uncovered in SCP-3008-1, it could

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:33.920
– in theory – be infinite.

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:38.280
Laser rangefinder tests, which are normally
very reliable, have only given inconclusive

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:39.280
results.

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:43.170
Interestingly, the anomalous area doesn’t
have any clear, visual differences from the

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:46.470
rest of the Ikea store except that it extends
forever.

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:51.640
An individual trapped within the confines
of SCP-3008-1 wouldn’t even realize that

00:07:51.640 --> 00:07:55.960
they’d entered an anomalous zone until they
tried to locate an exit and leave, at which

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:58.920
point, they’d find they were already hopelessly
lost.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:04.020
The geography of SCP-3008-1 does at least
appear to be consistent, so people trapped

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:08.400
within are theoretically able to retrace their
steps and escape if they hadn’t already

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:09.750
ventured too deep.

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:14.890
According to data collected during the drone
reconnaissance missions, SCP-3008-2, of which

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:19.460
there appeared to be a vast population, would
wander the stores aimlessly during the day.

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:23.640
They were unresponsive to the drone’s presence,
and did not appear to be aggressive.

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:27.490
While the physical descriptions of these creatures
could vary slightly, they all followed the

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:33.060
same overall trend: “Clothes” consistent
with the Ikea uniform, no face, either seemingly

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:37.630
too tall or too short, and limbs that are
grossly out of proportion with their bodies.

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:43.229
As the Foundation began sending drones deeper
into SCP-3008-1, they found another incredible

00:08:43.229 --> 00:08:44.229
discovery.

00:08:44.229 --> 00:08:48.350
There was an unknown population of humans
trapped inside the Ikea’s anomalous zone,

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:52.790
and these people had used the Ikea furniture
around them to create entire settlements and

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:54.450
towns within the store.

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:58.269
There were several of these towns, all of
which seemed to cohabitate peacefully.

00:08:58.269 --> 00:09:02.699
Even Foundation personnel found this development
in their research to be truly extraordinary.

00:09:02.699 --> 00:09:07.970
Since SCP-3008 was first identified, there
have been only fourteen civilian escapes.

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:12.300
Some had been trapped inside for months, others
had been in there for years – some far longer

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:14.129
than Martin’s three-year stint.

00:09:14.129 --> 00:09:18.279
While every one of these escapees has eventually
been released back to their home, after a

00:09:18.279 --> 00:09:22.999
liberal application of Amnestics and a proper
cover story has been devised, the Foundation

00:09:22.999 --> 00:09:25.329
interviewed each of them extensively first.

00:09:25.329 --> 00:09:30.000
According to these escapees, the people trapped
inside the Ikea have built an entirely new

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.700
society across the various settlements.

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:36.870
Contrary to the “Lord of the Flies” expectations
of a group of people isolated and afraid,

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:39.999
there’s immense cooperation between the
trapped civilians.

00:09:39.999 --> 00:09:45.569
The food in the several Ikea restaurants in
SCP-3008-1 mysteriously replenishes while

00:09:45.569 --> 00:09:48.560
nobody is there, so there’s no threat of
starving.

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:52.790
And the automatic turning on and off of the
lights forms a kind of rudimentary day and

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:53.870
night cycle.

00:09:53.870 --> 00:09:59.300
Night time, however, is when things get dangerous,
as the SCP-3008-2 entities – which are known

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:03.610
to the people inside as “The Staff” – become
extremely hostile after dark.

00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:08.550
Aggressive hordes of the Staff swarm the settlements
at night, repeating “The store is now closed,

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:09.800
please exit the building.”

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:14.079
The civilians inside are usually able to repel
these attacks with minimal casualties, but

00:10:14.079 --> 00:10:17.300
the constant war of attrition slowly wears
down those inside.

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:21.220
The bodies of the creatures also need to be
removed from the area after each attack, as

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:25.240
the presence of corpses or even parts of corpses
has been known to heighten the ferocity of

00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:26.689
the next night’s attack.

00:10:26.689 --> 00:10:30.749
During the day, the Staff return to a docile
and unresponsive state, though they’ll still

00:10:30.749 --> 00:10:34.009
defend themselves violently if anyone dares
to attack.

00:10:34.009 --> 00:10:37.580
Over the course of the interviews with the
fourteen escapees, Foundation Researchers

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:42.230
were able to answer another of their key questions:
How had so many people gone missing in the

00:10:42.230 --> 00:10:45.069
store for so long without being noticed?

00:10:45.069 --> 00:10:48.800
But the answer they received only raised many
more unsettling queries.

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:52.680
According to the escapees, there were people
inside the settlements that, despite being

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:57.670
otherwise of entirely sound mind and standard
intelligence, seemed to lack very common knowledge

00:10:57.670 --> 00:10:59.309
that even a child should know.

00:10:59.309 --> 00:11:04.050
For example, some weren’t aware of the International
Space Station orbiting the earth, or stranger

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:06.540
still, the existence of the Statue of Liberty.

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:12.139
This led the Researchers to a frightening
conclusion: SCP-3008-1 may not only be a nexus

00:11:12.139 --> 00:11:17.339
point of multiple Ikea stores in our dimension,
it could be connected to Ikeas in every dimension

00:11:17.339 --> 00:11:18.939
where Ikeas exist.

00:11:18.939 --> 00:11:22.360
While it only abducts a handful of people
from each store over an extended period of

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:27.269
time, it suddenly becomes clear how this SCP
was able to trap so many people without detection

00:11:27.269 --> 00:11:29.040
over such a long period of time.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:34.500
Which, in turn, led to an even more terrifying
revelation: The SCP Foundation may not have

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:38.310
SCP-3008-1 as contained as they thought.

00:11:38.310 --> 00:11:43.639
It might even be tucked away in an Ikea somewhere
near you, just waiting for you to visit.

00:11:43.639 --> 00:11:45.850
After all, there’s always room for one more…

